an unmasked frame                  -> close 1002, closed=1  client frames must be masked
text that is not UTF-8             -> close 1007, closed=1  invalid UTF-8 in a text message
a text with an overlong 'a'        -> close 1007, closed=1  invalid UTF-8 in a text message
reserved bit RSV1, no extension    -> close 1002, closed=1  unexpected RSV1 bit
unknown opcode 3                   -> close 1002, closed=1  unknown opcode
a ping that is fragmented          -> close 1002, closed=1  control frame is fragmented
a ping with 126 bytes              -> close 1002, closed=1  control frame too long
a continuation with no message     -> close 1002, closed=1  continuation without a message
length 126 used for 5 bytes        -> close 1002, closed=1  length not minimal
close with the code 1005           -> close 1002, closed=1  invalid close code
a close with a one byte payload    -> close 1002, closed=1  close frame with a one byte payload
11 bytes where 10 are allowed      -> close 1009, closed=1  frame too big
a frame announcing 1 TiB           -> close 1009, closed=1  frame too big
